menu "BurnScope display"

choice BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY
    prompt "Display profile"
    default BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY_CYD2USB_ST7789
    help
        Picks one panel-driver-plus-UI bundle. Each profile lives under
        `main/displays/<name>/` and owns both its panel bring-up and its
        LVGL layout because UI design is geometry-bound. To add a new
        screen, drop in displays/<name>/{driver.c,ui.c,Kconfig,sources.cmake}
        and append one rsource line below.

    rsource "displays/cyd2usb_st7789/Kconfig"
    rsource "displays/amoled_co5300/Kconfig"

endchoice

endmenu
